## Code Style
- Use type hints on all functions
- Prefer composition over inheritance
- Maximum line length: 100 characters
- Use dataclasses for simple data containers
- Use f-strings over .format() or % formatting

## Testing
- Every public function needs at least one test
- Use pytest, not unittest
- Test edge cases and error conditions
- Aim for 80% code coverage minimum

## Git
- Commit messages: imperative mood, 50 char subject line
- Feature branches off main
- Squash merge to main

## Architecture
- No circular imports
- Use dependency injection over globals
- Separate concerns: data, logic, presentation

## Module Size (Tiered)
- Standard tier (300 lines max): application logic, agents, tools, CLI, stateful code
- Extended tier (500 lines max): DSL primitives, data loaders, pure utility modules
- Hard ceiling: NO file may exceed 500 lines, period
- Extended tier requires: pure functions only, single semantic domain, full test coverage
- See DSL_FILE_SIZE_RESEARCH.md for rationale and references

## Security
- Never execute commands without safety checking
- Always validate user input before processing
- Never store secrets in source code
- Log all tool executions for audit trail
